# An allowlist, because of what the two excluded things cost. `.env` and `.env.<event>` must never
# reach a layer — secrets arrive by `--env-file` at run time (ADR-0008) — and an allowlist means a
# later `COPY` cannot widen onto one by accident. `.git/`, `.cache/`, `state/` and `runs/` are the
# rest of this repository by volume, and none of it is the image's business — `runs/` least of all,
# since a promoted Step stream is what the image *produces* and never something it reads.
*
!solver

# The assembled Tool-supply is the only part of its source tree that belongs in the image. The
# lock and fixture stay host-side inputs; the generated rootfs and its audit records are the
# reproducible output copied below.
!tool-supply
tool-supply/*
!tool-supply/generated
tool-supply/generated/*
!tool-supply/generated/rootfs
!tool-supply/generated/rootfs/**
!tool-supply/generated/apt-packages.txt
!tool-supply/generated/inventory.json
!tool-supply/generated/receipt.json
!tool-supply/generated/capabilities.json

# Git retains only the executable class of committed modes. This build-only helper restores the
# exact modes from the validated generated inventory after its rootfs crosses that boundary.
!scripts
scripts/*
!scripts/apply_tool_supply_modes.py
!scripts/deterministic_recovery_qualification.py
!scripts/runtime_qualification.py
!scripts/verify_sage_closure.py

# The third thing ADR-0008 bakes in: every event's tracked Board profile, which `CTFD_URL` selects
# between at run time. Written out one directory at a time rather than as a single `!` line, because
# a re-inclusion whose parent is excluded is the shape that silently ships nothing — and a missing
# profile is a container that refuses to start with a human already gone home.
!docs
docs/*
!docs/competitions
docs/competitions/*
!docs/competitions/*.board.json

# Byte-compiled leftovers of whatever interpreter last ran on the host — not the one in the image.
solver/**/__pycache__
solver/**/__pycache__/**
solver/**/*.pyc
